# OODOS's disk formats, for cpmtools (mkfs.cpm, cpmls, cpmcp, cpmrm, fsck.cpm).
# Point cpmtools at this file with -f and DISKDEFS (see oodos/README.md), or
# add these entries to its own diskdefs. All are CP/M 3 ("os 3") formats with
# 512-byte sectors, the SD card's, and no boot tracks: OODOS loads from
# /BOOT.BIN on the FAT card, so a drive image is all file system. Apple CP/M
# disks use cpmtools's own "apple-do", the SoftCard's format. hw/oodos.md has
# the reasons.

# The usual SD drive: 8 MB.
diskdef oodos-8m
  seclen 512
  tracks 1024
  sectrk 16
  blocksize 4096
  maxdir 1024
  skew 0
  boottrk 0
  os 3
end

# A large SD drive: 32 MB.
diskdef oodos-32m
  seclen 512
  tracks 4096
  sectrk 16
  blocksize 8192
  maxdir 2048
  skew 0
  boottrk 0
  os 3
end

# M:, the RAM disk in banks C-D (128 KB). OODOS makes it at boot; this is for
# tests and for looking at a saved copy.
diskdef oodos-ram
  seclen 512
  tracks 16
  sectrk 16
  blocksize 2048
  maxdir 256
  skew 0
  boottrk 0
  os 3
end
